This test races the MDI queue on purpose: the subroutine does a tool change
and then reads #5400, so the expected output only holds when the change has
finished and the interpreter has resynced before the parameter is read.  That
outcome depends on real timing, and a second session on the same machine
changes it: run alongside anything it reports the previous tool at a couple
of the switch points.  It has the machine to itself so it keeps testing the
queue and not the load.
